{"name":"Blackout","hex":"#0e0702","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blackout","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A temporary loss of consciousness.","A temporary loss of memory."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative form of black out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackout"}],"entries":[{"title":"Power outage","blocks":[{"text":"A power outage, also called a blackout, a power failure, a power blackout, a power loss, a power cut, a power out or a power drought is the complete loss of the electrical power network supply to an end user."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Calle_Larga_at_night_during_power_cut.jpg/330px-Calle_Larga_at_night_during_power_cut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_outage"},{"title":"Blackout (broadcasting)","blocks":[{"text":"In broadcasting, the term blackout refers to the non-airing of television or radio programming in a certain media market."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackout_(broadcasting)"},{"title":"Blackout (Britney Spears album)","blocks":[{"text":"Blackout is the fifth studio album by American singer Britney Spears. It was released on October 25, 2007, by Jive Records. Its production and release occurred as Spears' personal struggles were highly publicized and overshadowed her professional projects. She executive-produced the album, working with producers Danja, Bloodshy & Avant, Sean Garrett, and the Neptunes, among others; it is the only album on which Spears is credited as the executive producer. The final result was primarily a dance-pop and electropop record with R&B, Euro disco and dubstep influences, with lyrical themes revolving around love, fame, media scrutiny, sex, and clubbing."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/76/Britney_Spears_-_Blackout.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackout_(Britney_Spears_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Crossed_wires.JPG/500px-Crossed_wires.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Crossed_wires.JPG/500px-Crossed_wires.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tree limbs creating a short circuit in power lines during a storm on July 21, 2006. This typically results in a power outage in the area supplied by these lines","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrossed_wires.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/V4_Web_BOeLL-FF_Energiewende_%28page_8_crop%29_-_Stromausfall.jpg/500px-V4_Web_BOeLL-FF_Energiewende_%28page_8_crop%29_-_Stromausfall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/V4_Web_BOeLL-FF_Energiewende_%28page_8_crop%29_-_Stromausfall.jpg/1280px-V4_Web_BOeLL-FF_Energiewende_%28page_8_crop%29_-_Stromausfall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/V4_Web_BOeLL-FF_Energiewende_%28page_8_crop%29_-_Stromausfall.jpg/500px-V4_Web_BOeLL-FF_Energiewende_%28page_8_crop%29_-_Stromausfall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Comparison of duration of power outages (SAIDI value), in 2014. Note this chart is in German.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AV4_Web_BOeLL-FF_Energiewende_(page_8_crop)_-_Stromausfall.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/You_Want_a_Piece_of_Me%3F_%283526044353%29.jpg/500px-You_Want_a_Piece_of_Me%3F_%283526044353%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia